@model CommunityHub.Forms.Steps.SponsorLogosModel
@*
    Fields-ONLY partial for the sponsor Logos wizard step (§32 / §285 Phase 2). Two file inputs —
    the shared wizard host form is multipart. Field names match SponsorLogosModel. §297: each input
    shows the CURRENTLY uploaded file for that logo (file inputs can't be pre-filled), from the
    per-kind upload audit, so a coordinator can see what's already there. Upload replaces it
    (versioned); the step completes only when BOTH are present.

    §6.7 / §768.14 — the third input, "Logo for the Event System (Zoho) lead system", is gone. One
    Web PNG now serves both the promotion graphics and the external event system, so we stopped
    asking a sponsor to upload the same logo twice into two folders we then had to keep in step.
*@
@{
    string CurrentLine(string? name) => string.IsNullOrEmpty(name)
        ? "No file uploaded yet"
        : "Uploaded: " + name;
    string CurrentColor(string? name) => string.IsNullOrEmpty(name) ? "#b45309" : "#15803d";
}

<p style="font-size:13.5px;color:#4b5563;margin-top:0;">
    Upload both logos. Each is versioned automatically — the latest file is always the one we use,
    and re-uploading replaces the current one. The step is complete once both are uploaded.
</p>
@* §783.4 — THERE IS NOW AN UPLOAD BUTTON, and it reports progress.
   Operator 2026-08-03: "i am missing an upload button … problem is that the system hangs for 6
   seconds when you click next so it is not user friendly. i prefer a buttn and it must show that it
   is uploading etc. Use same functionality as for exhibitor wall upload or speaker preview/final
   presentation upload".

   🔒 §473 answered this SAME complaint with a paragraph saying no button exists. That explained the
   surprise without removing it, and left a six-second upload with no feedback at all — which is how
   somebody concludes it has hung and presses again.

   It is a submit carrying `__dir=stay`, NOT a nested <form> (§304b — a nested form does not post at
   all). Same progressive enhancement as _PresentationUpload: it posts normally with JavaScript off;
   the script only disables the button and relabels it, so a slow upload looks busy, not broken. *@
@if (TempData["WizardStepSaved"] is string wss)
{
    <p role="status" style="margin:0 0 12px;padding:8px 12px;border-radius:8px;background:#ecfdf5;color:#065f46;border:1px solid #a7f3d0;font-size:13.5px;">@wss</p>
}

<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin:0 0 14px;">
    <p style="font-size:13px;color:#4b5563;margin:0 0 8px;">
        Choose your files below, then press <strong>Upload logos now</strong>. A large file takes a
        few seconds &mdash; the button says so while it works, and stays on this step so you can see
        the result.
    </p>
    <button type="submit" name="__dir" value="stay" formnovalidate class="task-act task-act--primary"
            onclick="var f=this.form; if(f.__stayMsg){f.__stayMsg.value='Your logos were uploaded.';}
                     var b=this;
                     setTimeout(function(){ b.disabled=true; b.style.opacity='0.75';
                        b.innerHTML='<span class=&quot;ceh-spin&quot;></span> Uploading&hellip; please keep this page open'; }, 0);
                     return true;">
        &#11014;&#65039; Upload logos now
    </button>
</div>

<label for="SoMeLogo">Logo for Web <span style="color:#6b7280;font-weight:400;">(PNG, max 5 MB)</span></label>
@* 🔴 §1143b — SAME REQUIREMENT AS /Sponsor/CompanyDetails, AND IT MUST BE ON BOTH.
   This wizard step and the company page are two doors onto ONE upload; stating the rule on only
   one of them is the §730 stale-copy trap — the sponsor who used the other door would still send
   a knockout logo and still vanish from the promotion graphic. *@
<p style="color:#8a5a00;background:#fff8e6;border:1px solid #f0dcb8;border-radius:6px;
          padding:9px 12px;font-size:12.5px;margin:2px 0 8px;">
    <strong>Please upload the POSITIVE version</strong> — the one made for <strong>light
    backgrounds</strong> (dark or full-colour artwork). We place it on a <strong>white panel</strong>,
    so a white / reversed “knockout” logo becomes <strong>invisible</strong>. A transparent
    background is fine — it is the <em>colour of the logo itself</em> that matters.
</p>
<input type="file" id="SoMeLogo" name="SoMeLogo" accept=".png,image/png" />
<p style="font-size:12px;color:@CurrentColor(Model.CurrentSoMeFileName);margin:2px 0 12px;">@(string.IsNullOrEmpty(Model.CurrentSoMeFileName) ? "○ " : "✓ ")@CurrentLine(Model.CurrentSoMeFileName)</p>
<span asp-validation-for="SoMeLogo" class="error"></span>

<label for="PrintLogo">Logo for Print <span style="color:#6b7280;font-weight:400;">(vector: .eps, .ai or .pdf, max 25 MB)</span></label>
<input type="file" id="PrintLogo" name="PrintLogo" accept=".eps,.ai,.pdf" />
<p style="font-size:12px;color:@CurrentColor(Model.CurrentPrintFileName);margin:2px 0 12px;">@(string.IsNullOrEmpty(Model.CurrentPrintFileName) ? "○ " : "✓ ")@CurrentLine(Model.CurrentPrintFileName)</p>
<span asp-validation-for="PrintLogo" class="error"></span>
